Flag a passage only when mixing a procedure, prerequisites, exceptions, rationale, and verification conditions materially obstructs reading. Identify the mixed information types and a grouping that preserves every stated requirement. Prefer the main procedure first, followed by conditions ordered by impact. A short definition or linear explanation needs no restructuring.

Specifications should state current design rationale, not a chronological work log. Flag history only when it displaces the present contract or its reason.
